# Dashboard UI & Design Tokens

## Layout Density & Spacing
- Use compact, high-density spacing tokens. Dashboard cards should use tight padding (`p-4` to `p-6`).
- Grid Layouts: Standardize on a responsive 12-column grid system (`grid grid-cols-12 gap-4`).
- Card Consistency: Every dashboard widget must sit inside a uniform `Card` container featuring subtle borders, background contrast, and standardized rounded corners (`rounded-xl border border-border bg-card`).

## Color System & Visual Status
- Semantic Indicators: Use semantic colors exclusively for dynamic statuses (Success: Green, Warning: Amber, Error: Red, Neutral: Slate/Zinc).
- Dark Mode Native: Ensure all layout background and text classes utilize CSS variables or Tailwind dark mode utilities (`bg-background text-foreground`).
- Never use raw hex values (`#1e293b`). Use design tokens (`bg-muted/50`, `border-border/60`).

## Tables & Lists
- Wrap data tables inside responsive overflow shells (`overflow-x-auto`).
- Use sticky headers (`sticky top-0`) for long tabular lists.